# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json

### 2. Component Integration
- Modified `/src/App.tsx` to import and include the SpeedInsights component
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the App component's JSX

## Framework Identification
The project was identified as a **React + Vite** application based on:
- Vite configuration in `vite.config.ts` with React plugin
- Main entry point at `src/main.tsx` using React's `createRoot`
- Project structure following React conventions

Following the official documentation, the React-specific integration path was used (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`).

## Verification Steps Completed
✅ TypeScript compilation successful (no errors)
✅ Build process verified (npm run build)
✅ Linter check passed (npm run lint)
✅ Dependencies properly updated in package.json
✅ package-lock.json generated with correct dependency tree

## Files Modified
- `src/App.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Generated/updated with new dependency

## Next Steps
Once this is deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
2. Data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights
3. The component will inject the necessary tracking scripts automatically
4. No additional configuration is required for basic functionality

## Notes
- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and won't affect page performance
- It only loads and reports data when deployed on Vercel
- The implementation follows React best practices and preserves existing code structure
- All existing functionality remains intact
